     2	# verify-counts.sh — PLAN-087 W-F.3 + PLAN-112-FOLLOWUP-claude-md-count-drift —
     3	# README/INSTALL/CLAUDE.md numeric-claim drift detector (bidirectional).
     4	#
     5	# Derives the canonical counts at runtime and compares them to the values
     6	# cited in the framework's top-level docs (CLAUDE.md, README.md, INSTALL.md).
     7	# Reports drift as one violation per line; exits 0 on full parity, 1 on any
     8	# drift.
     9	#
    10	# Usage:
    11	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/verify-counts.sh              # human report + exit code
    12	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/verify-counts.sh --quiet      # exit code only
    13	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/verify-counts.sh --json       # machine-readable JSON
    14	#   bash .claude/scripts/local/verify-counts.sh --no-tests   # skip the slow pytest collect
    15	#
    16	# =====================  COUNT CONTRACT (W1, S160/S161)  =====================
    17	# Each metric below is derived from a single live source of truth and then
    18	# checked against EVERY occurrence in the watched docs (all-matches, NOT
    19	# head -1). Three rule kinds:
    20	#   - exact  : the doc number MUST equal the live count.
    21	#   - floor  : the doc states "N+"; the live count MUST be >= N (so adding a
    22	#              test never churns the docs — AC6).
    23	#   - approx : the doc states a ROUNDED figure ("~14,000 collected cases",
    24	#              "~730 test files"). See the APPROX CONTRACT block below.
    25	# The check is BIDIRECTIONAL (a doc number that disagrees with live fails)
    26	# and CROSS-FILE (each doc is checked against the live value, so all docs are
    27	# mutually consistent by transitivity — AC3/AC4).
    28	#
    29	#   metric            live source                                   rule
    30	#   ----------------  --------------------------------------------  -----
    31	#   skills (total)    find .claude/skills -name SKILL.md            exact (166)
    32	#   core skills       find .claude/skills/core -name SKILL.md       exact (42)
    33	#   frontend skills   find .claude/skills/frontend -name SKILL.md   exact (8)
    34	#   domain skills     find .claude/skills/domains -name SKILL.md    exact (116)
    35	#   ADRs              ls .claude/adr/ADR-*.md                        exact (190)
    36	#   hook .py files    ls .claude/hooks/*.py                          exact (57)
    37	#   registered hooks  distinct *.py in settings.json hooks{} tree   exact (46)
    38	#   registrations     total hook entries in settings.json hooks{}   exact (48)
    39	#   _lib modules      ls .claude/hooks/_lib/*.py  (TOP-LEVEL glob)   exact (68)
    40	#   SPEC v1 files     ls SPEC/v1/*.md                                exact (32)
    41	#   tests             pytest --collect-only -q  (DOCUMENTED scope)  floor (N+) + approx (~N)
    42	#   test_files        git ls-files '*test_*.py' '*_test.py'         approx (~N)
    43	#   release_steps     grep -c '      - name:' release.yml           exact (31)
    44	#   commands          find .claude/commands -name '*.md'             exact (27)
    45	#   workflows         find .github/workflows -name '*.yml'           exact (22)
    46	#   mutation_fixtures find tests/formal_verification/mutation_...    exact (85)
    47	#   tla_specs         ls docs/formal-verification/*.tla              exact (4)
    48	#
    49	# =====================  APPROX CONTRACT (PLAN-166 W0 F5)  ===================
    50	# WHY a third kind. Two doc claims are deliberately ROUNDED because the exact
    51	# figure churns on every commit: the collected-case count and the test-file
    52	# count. `exact` would make every new test rewrite six documents; `floor`
    53	# only catches OVERSELL ("docs say 12k, live is 11k") and is blind to
    54	# UNDERSELL — and undersell is precisely the drift observed in the rc.1
    55	# re-pass (npm/README.md, docs/FAQ.md and README.pt-BR.md all sat at
    56	# "~12,000" while the live collect had grown past 14,000; the `floor` rule
    57	# happily reported "no drift" the whole time because 14172 >= 12000).
    58	#
    59	# THE RULE, stated in full:
    60	#   1. BAND. The cited figure, normalized to an integer ("~14,000" / "~14.000"
    61	#      / "~14k" all -> 14000), must sit within +/- 5% of the live value.
    62	#      5% of the collected-case count is ~700 cases, which is why (2) exists.
    63	#   2. CROSS-DOC EQUALITY. Every watched doc must cite the SAME normalized
    64	#      figure for a given approx metric. A pure band check is not enough:
    65	#      "~720 test files" (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) and "~730 test files"
    66	#      (CLAUDE.md) were BOTH inside a 5% band of the live 736 while
    67	#      contradicting each other in public — a live divergence between two
    68	#      watched docs that the gate could not see. Equality makes the release
    69	#      restate one number, not a range.
    70	#   3. INPUTS ARE PRINTED. A band without its inputs is a licence to drift:
    71	#      +/-700 cases can hide an entire test family. The gate prints, for every
    72	#      approx metric, the exact command used, the observed value, and — for
    73	#      the collect-driven metric — the COLLECTION-ERROR COUNT. errors > 0 is
    74	#      a VIOLATION whenever the band was actually enforced over >=1 doc site
    75	#      this run: the observed count is then measured over a PARTIAL population
    76	#      and a band verdict over the wrong number is untrustworthy — and the
    77	#      automated callers (validate.yml --quiet; the release preflight, which
    78	#      discards output) can only see the exit code, so a warning there is
    79	#      structurally invisible (PLAN-166 W0 re-pass). It stays a named WARNING
    80	#      only when the band is already suspended (--no-tests / observed 0).
    81	#
    82	# COLLECTION SCOPE (load-bearing — the two populations DIVERGE). This block
    83	# is the ONLY measurement snapshot in this file (W0 re-pass round 2: two
    84	# divergent pairs coexisted, one undated — the numeral-espelho class; a
    85	# reader could not tell which measurement backed the scope decision).
    86	# Measured 2026-08-06 on the PLAN-166 W0 tree AFTER the residual-fix round
    87	# (the previous snapshot went stale within its own patch — the residual
    88	# fixers added tests after it was pasted; codex W0-residuals round caught
    89	# it). Both figures are OUTPUTS of the two commands, pasted, not recalled:
    90	#   `python3 -m pytest --collect-only -q`            -> 14263 tests,  0 errors
    91	#   `python3 -m pytest --collect-only -q .claude/`   -> 14310 tests, 22 errors
