    77	CONTEXT
    78	- Repo: ceo-orchestration, a governance/auditability framework. Python
    79	  stdlib-only, >=3.9. No speed claims anywhere.
    80	- $RC_TAG is CUT, signed, CI-green, published as a GitHub pre-release,
    81	  under a signed pair-rail verdict (GO-WITH-CONDITIONS).
    82	- Review history you must NOT re-litigate: 4 pre-rc.1 rounds (18
    83	  findings, 17 fixed 1 refuted) + 4 multi-part rounds rc.1->rc.2
    84	  (all real findings cured in fix-forwards; final candidate green).
    85	- FOUR NAMED PRODUCT EXCEPTIONS ride this GA by signed decision
    86	  (V1/V2/V4/V5 - upgrade.sh observer w/o baseline-invalid guard; false
    87	  --pin NOTE; rejected-symlink hash fallthrough; FMS_LINK_PATHS unset
    88	  allow-all on install). Cures are STAGED in a post-GA ceremony pack.
    89	  Do NOT report these as new; DO report if any is WORSE than described
    90	  or reachable on the mainline install/upgrade path (they were assessed
    91	  as non-mainline).
    92	- OWN-0016 is a known gated defect (ADR-190 s2.6, expected nightly RED).
    93	
    94	WHAT THIS HOLD RE-PASS IS FOR
    95	1. GA EXECUTABILITY: remaining path is bump --stable (expected no-op),
    96	   tag --stable, push (push triggers npm publish via OIDC). Anything
    97	   non-idempotent or order-dependent?
    98	2. IRREVERSIBILITY: what lands wrong on npm and cannot be undone?
    99	   Version-string disagreement across published surfaces is the
   100	   highest-value class.
   101	3. ADOPTER BLAST RADIUS: v1.2.0 adopter runs the documented upgrade
   102	   against v1.3.0 - broken/locked states?
   103	4. HONESTY OF CLAIMS: every count/guarantee in the changed docs must
   104	   match the code at the tag. A gate that cannot fail is a finding.
   105	5. What a reviewer would most plausibly have missed across 8 rounds.
   106	
   107	OUTPUT FORMAT
   108	Per finding: SEVERITY (P0 blocks GA / P1 fix before GA / P2 follow-up),
   109	FILE:LINE, concrete failure scenario, minimal fix. Cite the diff.
   110	End with exactly one line: "VERDICT: GO" or "VERDICT: NO-GO" or
